From 7bbaad1dc1c675c8a601f9aed004584506702c8a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 08:15:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/11] edge: opt-in near-duplicate roots, so echoes of one
 event at a site are one root

egress.near_duplicate_roots {jaccard, days} (optional; absent = the shipped
exact-text rule, same pack bytes and hash). A record with no origin and no
exact folded-text match shares the root of the earliest earlier record at the
same site with the same entities, received within 'days', whose folded word
set overlaps by at least 'jaccard'. Only the site's own roots change; nothing
new crosses the Boundary (it can only lower roots_bucket).

Why: the EMERGENCE narrative starts with the author line, so the exact rule
never fires on echoes: every echo of one event was an independent root
(decoy class 4, the same copied-root defect as MycelicLabs finding 2).
Dev seeds 0-5 at 0.65/14: every echo (site, event) group collapses to one
root; 2 of 3,912 true-pattern records merge with another record. Tuned on dev
seeds against the generator's near-duplicate echoes; effect on real text is
not measured.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
